==Battleground==
*1 [[Titi Cat]] spawns as the boss after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*1 [[Wyvern (Enemy)|Wyvern]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*10 [[Fuu (Enemy)|Fuus]] spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[Hearscht (Enemy)|Hearscht]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since Titi has 350 Range, general midrange units will be outranged and killed before they can realistically do much. You'll instead need solid backliner Cats that can deal good damage over time. Some examples include [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] & his [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Counterpart]], [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bath Cat]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] can work, but she is much riskier to use than Bahamut as her Knockback can potentially cause your units to push into [[Wyvern (Enemy)|Wyvern's]] range and be killed due to his high damage. As for meatshields, fast ones like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] & [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]] combined with the usual ones like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] should be enough. If you happen to have [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], this stage is pretty much free as long as you protect him properly, since he outranges every single enemy in the stage and can chip them down and slow them. Other useful units include [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], with high health and decent DPS, [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] as a decent no-gacha alternative to Cyberpunk, and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] to chip Titi and the other backliners by using the occasional [[Fuu (Enemy)|Fuu]] as a stepping stone for its waves.

